// docs/assembly.md, architecture.md, bootstrap.md, benchmarks.md content.
page("docs/assembly.md",[h(1,"Assembly card"),
  "`@asm` + indented instructions; no block punctuation or instruction strings needed. Optional header qualifiers: `volatile`, `inline`, `goto`.",
  code("c",["@f add5(int x) int","  int y","  @asm","    movl %[src],%[dst]","    addl $5,%[dst]","    out [dst] \"=&r\"(y)","    in [src] \"r\"(x)","    clobber \"cc\"","  y"]),
  "Example targets x86. NanoC forwards instructions to the target assembler unchanged. Each raw instruction gets a newline; quoted C strings are accepted verbatim too. Optional sections, once each, in this order:",
  tbl(["Word","Payload"],[[c("out"),"C output constraints, e.g. `\"+r\"(x), \"=m\"(memory)`"],[c("in"),"C input constraints, e.g. `\"r\"(x), \"i\"(42)`"],
    [c("clobber"),"Changed registers, `\"cc\"`, `\"memory\"`"],[c("labels"),"C jump labels; requires `@asm goto`"]]),
  "Supports named operands, fixed-register constraints, matching operands, early clobbers and compiler attributes through ordinary C. Emits `__asm__`; requires a GNU-assembly backend (GCC/Clang tested). Instruction set, ABI and dialect belong to the target compiler (e.g. `-masm=intel`). `volatile` retains side effects; `\"memory\"` is a compiler barrier, not a hardware fence. "+link("Backend contract","https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Extended-Asm.html")+"."])
dirs:=[["include/nanoc","Internal subsystem contracts, written in NanoC (types only; prototypes are generated)"],
  ["bootstrap","Generated frozen C seed, including main and its own headers"],
  ["src/frontend","Tokens, cursors, declarations, native `@f`, recursive expansion"],["src/macros","Templates, captures, program macros"],
  ["src/eval","Values, scopes, checked arithmetic, expressions, executable programs"],
  ["src/meta","Builtin registry, source passes, text/list edits, BT host operations"],
  ["src/support","Aligned arenas, maps, buffers, diagnostics, atomic files"],["src/cli","Options, compact catalogs, JSON/text reporting"],
  ["src/layout","Indented runtime/meta bodies, short controls, implicit returns"],["src/emit","Pretty and mini C emitters"],
  ["src/dsl","Shared generator DSLs (JSON, Markdown, files) for `*.bt.nc` programs"],
  ["src/dsl/ui.bt.nc, src/web/ui, src/web/pages","Website widgets: one tree per widget with element-level `css`, `js` and `on` blocks; classes and script ids are generated, `[as=name]` reaches an element as `A.name`"],
  ["src/content/*.doc.nc","Prose, tables and runnable examples written once; rendered to `docs/*.md` and the website, with C produced by the live compiler"],
  ["src/wasm","The compiler's browser build (freestanding shim), also written in NanoC"],
  ["src/*.bt.nc, src/site, src/docs","Build-time generators: headers, editors, docs, website"],
  ["build.c, src/build.bt.nc","`build.c` compiles the C seed; the build workflow is NanoC"],["src/tests, tests/","NanoC test sources (built to C by ./builder test); corpus and fixtures data. Compiler behavior, real C, CLI/ABI/BT/install; `tests/corpus` is licensed upstream C"]]
page("docs/architecture.md",[h(1,"Implementation map"),
  "Self-hosted NanoC; C11 bootstrap; POSIX host, libc only. Sources <= "+LIMIT+" lines.",
  tbl(["Directory","Owns"],dirs),
  "Tokens are immutable source slices; lookahead copies indices. A context owns translation allocations and persistent pass state. Error checkpoints release all owned memory; arena accounting and budgets bound work. No-`@` input passes through. Output files use same-directory temporary files + rename. Host commands use argv; only explicit `sh` invokes a shell. Builtin signatures live in `src/meta/registry.nc`.",
  h(2,"Style"),
  ul(["`src/**/*.nc`: "+LIMIT+" lines per file; every file starts with a `//` header; every `@f` has a one-line `//` doc comment.",
    "Headers are generated: `include/nanoc/*.nc` (types) plus `nanoc --prototypes` per module, via `src/headers.bt.nc`.",
    "`*.bt.nc` files are build-time programs and are not compiler modules.",
    "Docs and editors are generated: `./builder docs`, `src/editors.bt.nc`."]),
  h(2,"Emitters"),
  ul(["`src/emit/pretty.nc`, `braces.nc`, `output.nc`: normal mode. A token pass over generated C: indentation, cuddled `else`, `case` indent, one blank line between top-level definitions, soft wrap at 90 columns.",
    "`src/emit/mini.nc`: `--emit mini` strips comments and layout; only directives keep their lines.",
    "Pure C with no real `@` use is returned unchanged in normal mode.",
    "Reseed after a formatting change: `NC_RESEED=1 ./builder snapshot` (twice), then `./builder bootstrap`."])])
page("docs/bootstrap.md",[h(1,"Bootstrap card"),
  "Requirements: POSIX host + C11 compiler. No installed NanoC, packages or downloads.",
  code("sh",["cc -std=c11 -O2 build.c -o builder","./builder bootstrap","./build/nanoc --version","./builder test","CC=clang ./builder test --sanitize"]),
  tbl(["Stage","Built from","Emits"],[[c("build/stage0"),"Frozen `bootstrap/src` C + `bootstrap/include`","`build/stage1/src` C"],
    [c("build/stage1-nanoc"),"Stage 1 C, generated from `src` NanoC","`build/stage2/src` C"],
    [c("build/nanoc"),"Stage 2 C, generated by self-hosted NanoC","`build/stage3/src` C"]]),
  "Every module's stage 1, 2 and 3 emitted C must match byte for byte. `build` caches verified builds by source/header/seed contents, compiler and sanitizer mode. `bootstrap` forces the complete chain. `clean` removes all stages.",
  code("sh",["./builder snapshot    # verify, then regenerate the committed C seed + frozen headers","./builder bootstrap   # prove the regenerated seed builds the same compiler"]),
  "Seed C is generated and frozen; do not maintain a second implementation. Every committed source, including seed files, stays at most "+LIMIT+" physical lines."])
page("docs/benchmarks.md",[h(1,"Measurement"),
  "`./builder bench` retains CSV and 10,000-function corpora in `build/bench-data`. Cases: plain C, native syntax, legacy shorthand/indentation, macros. Reports five warm in-process rounds, CLI elapsed time, peak RSS (GNU time), 20-launch startup. Plain C is passthrough, not parsing. C compilation is excluded. Report CPU, OS, compiler and flags when comparing; synthetic results are not universal speed claims."])
